# Warehouse initialization and upgrade workload.
#
# Copy to $AUTONOX_HOME/warehouse.env — not into this repo — and point the
# runner at it:
#   WAREHOUSE_ENV_FILE=$AUTONOX_HOME/warehouse.env ./run.sh upgrade-workspace
#
# Only settings that differ from run.sh's defaults are listed here. Those
# defaults are CONTAINER_RUNTIME=docker (set podman where appropriate),
# CONTAINER_MOUNT_SUFFIX empty (set :Z on SELinux hosts),
# WAREHOUSE_WIRING_PATH=/config/warehouse-wiring.yaml, and
# WAREHOUSE_CANONICAL_WIRING_PATH=/config/warehouse-canonical-wiring.yaml.

# Required: the autonox-warehouse image pinned for this customer environment.
# Each environment upgrades on its own cadence, so there is no repo-wide default.
#
# Prefer pinning it once in $AUTONOX_HOME/images.env — written by
# images/resolve-digests.sh and read by both this workload and the import
# workload, so a migrate and an import cannot run different builds. run.sh
# sources that file first, so setting WAREHOUSE_IMAGE here overrides it; leave
# it commented unless this deployment needs to diverge deliberately.
# WAREHOUSE_IMAGE=registry.example/autonox-warehouse@sha256:...

# Required. Connection value referenced by the wiring documents. Quote it —
# this file is shell-sourced, and an unquoted password containing <, >, spaces,
# or other shell metacharacters will break parsing.
WAREHOUSE_POSTGRES_DSN="postgresql://noxop:CHANGE_ME@postgres:5432/autonox"

# Required by every command except `raw`. This is the single source of truth
# for the workspace: run.sh passes it as --workspace-id, which outranks the
# spec.workspace_id in warehouse-wiring.yaml. run.sh refuses to run when the
# two disagree, so keep the wiring document in step with this value.
WORKSPACE_ID=

# Host directory holding the wiring documents, mounted read-only at /config.
# Defaults to $AUTONOX_HOME/warehouse-config — set an absolute path outside
# this repo.
# On VM-backed Docker it must be under a path the VM mounts, or it mounts empty
# and the CLI reports WIRING_INPUT_NOT_FOUND.
WAREHOUSE_CONFIG_DIR=/etc/autonox/warehouse-config

# Optional, for example: autonox-local. Leave empty when the DSN resolves directly.
CONTAINER_NETWORK=

# Published AutoNox images currently target linux/amd64. Set this on Apple
# Silicon when Docker emulation is available; leave empty for native targets.
WAREHOUSE_PLATFORM=linux/amd64

# Set when the selected wiring expects this environment value.
WAREHOUSE_CANONICAL_SHARED_SCHEMA=shared

# Optional path, also inside /config, when wiring uses secret providers.
# WAREHOUSE_SECRETS_PROVIDERS_URI=file:///config/secrets-providers.yaml

# Additional environment-variable names required by a customer wiring document.
# Values must already be exported or present in this file.
# WAREHOUSE_EXTRA_ENV_VARS="EXAMPLE_CERT_PATH"
